<div class="hero-copy container"><span class="eyebrow"><i></i> Open source · Local first</span><h1>Your AI agents deserve<br><em>a place to work.</em></h1><p>Stavlos is a local-first harness for long-lived coding agents. Start a team, stay in the loop, and steer the work as it happens.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button dark" href="https://github.com/nicodes/stavlos">Get Stavlos <b>→</b></a><a class="button outline" href="#how">See how it works ↓</a></div></div>
<div class="terminal container"><header><span class="dots">● ● ●</span><span>stavlos — ~/projects/atlas</span><span>3 agents · local</span></header><div class="terminal-grid"><aside><small>YOUR STABLE</small><b>◆ &nbsp; architect <em>working</em></b><b>◇ &nbsp; api-explorer <em>idle</em></b><b>◇ &nbsp; test-runner <em>working</em></b><small>SESSION</small><b>atlas <em>· 14m</em></b></aside><div class="chat"><header><b># architect</b><span>general · gpt-5.4 · <strong>32%</strong></span></header><p><small>you</small>Map the auth flow, then have someone verify the API boundaries.</p><p><small>◆ architect</small>I’ll trace the flow and ask an explorer to verify the boundary contracts in parallel.</p><div class="tool">↗ &nbsp; agent_create <code>api-explorer</code><strong>running</strong></div><p><small>◆ architect</small>The session middleware owns refresh. I’m checking the handoff now<span class="cursor"></span></p><footer><b>›</b> Steer your agent… <kbd>enter</kbd></footer></div></div></div></section>
<section class="proof"><div class="container"><p>Built around how real work<br>actually unfolds.</p><div><b>Long-lived</b><span>Agents keep their context and return when you need them.</span></div><div><b>Steerable</b><span>Redirect work in flight without losing the thread.</span></div><div><b>Local-first</b><span>Your machine, your subscriptions, your control.</span></div></div></section>
<section class="how container" id="how"><div class="heading"><small>01 — The model</small><h2>Not a one-shot tool.<br>A <em>working relationship.</em></h2></div><div class="how-grid"><p>Most agent workflows end when a response lands. Stavlos starts there. Agents are persistent actors with an inbox, their own context, and the ability to collaborate.</p><div class="steps"><article><small>01</small><div><h3>Start with a conversation</h3><p>Open Stavlos in any project and talk to your root agent from the terminal.</p></div></article><article><small>02</small><div><h3>Build a team when it matters</h3><p>Your agent delegates focused work. Each child can report back, then remain available for follow-ups.</p></div></article><article><small>03</small><div><h3>Stay in the driver’s seat</h3><p>Prompt, steer, cancel, or kill any agent—at any point in the work.</p></div></article></div></div></section>
<section class="principles" id="principles"><div class="container"><div class="heading"><small>02 — Under the hood</small><h2>Calm on the surface.<br><em>Serious underneath.</em></h2></div><div class="cards"><article><span>↳</span><h3>One source of truth</h3><p>An append-only event log means every conversation, tool call, and state change can be resumed and replayed.</p></article><article><span>◌</span><h3>Clients are peers</h3><p>The terminal UI, your own client, and future surfaces all speak the same JSON-RPC protocol.</p></article><article><span>⌘</span><h3>Permission by design</h3><p>Stavlos works on your machine with explicit policies, project trust gates, and no surprise execution.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="closing container"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32"><path d="M7 24.5V9.5l9-5 9 5v15l-9 5zM7 9.5l9 5 9-5M16 14.5v15"/></svg><small>Your workhorses are waiting.</small><h2>Give your agents<br><em>a stable.</em></h2><a class="button dark" href="https://github.com/nicodes/stavlos">Get Stavlos on GitHub <b>→</b></a></section></main><footer class="footer container"><a class="brand" href="#top">◇ stavlos</a><span>Open source agent harness · Built in Go</span><a href="https://github.com/nicodes/stavlos">GitHub ↗</a></footer>
